contributions.text:
{
  "reading": "He asked for a non-Game-Changer way to find Krang or Smothering Tithe while still aiming at a first kill by turn 6. The tutors axis reads 0. But no measured source says a tutor is a clear upgrade. Across three paired screens a working tutor beat a dead card by about 3.5-3.9 damage @T10 and nothing on killed-by-T6. If he wants one anyway, Long-Term Plans is the pick, because it is the only non-GC candidate that reaches both Krang and Tithe. A tutor does not move the turn-6 kill.",
  "log_entries_read": ["003", "004", "006", "008", "009"],
  "axes_engaged": [
    {"axis": "tutors", "verdict": "adequate", "measured": {"value": 0}, "reading": "Zero tutors, but the frame's '4-8 tutors' is the combo row and this is a draw-engine deck with 25 card-advantage copies."},
    {"axis": "card-advantage", "verdict": "strength", "measured": {"value": 25}, "reading": "The draw density is what makes a third-from-top tutor nearly a to-hand tutor: Brainstorm and all four wheels draw it."},
    {"axis": "power", "verdict": "adequate", "measured": {"value": 3}, "reading": "Three of three Game Changers. Enlightened Tutor would be a fourth, so it is out."}
  ],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Enduring Curiosity", "why": "Today's Krang screen read it as the cheapest draw engine to lose. It only draws off combat damage, and that overlaps Mask, Mastermind and the sharks.", "cost_of_cutting": "A flash, recurring draw engine. Krang doubles its draws, so each one is two Shabraz counters. Swapping it for each tutor read killed by T6 -0.9 to -1.0 pts, damage @T10 -8.0 to -11.9 and extra cards by T8 -0.7 to -0.9, all worse (goldfish).", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "contested"}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [
    {"card": "Long-Term Plans", "closes": "tutors", "source": "prompt", "why": "An instant that reaches any card: Krang, Tithe, Sphinx, a wheel. Third from the top is drawn within about a turn on this list (Brainstorm, wheels, Rhystic). The risk is the 4 fetchlands, which shuffle it away. Not a Game Changer.", "natural_cut": "Enduring Curiosity"},
    {"card": "Fabricate", "closes": "tutors", "source": "prompt", "why": "To hand, so it is immune to wheels and fetches. But it is artifact-only: Krang, Monument, Leng, Lizard Blades, Sol Ring. It cannot reach Tithe.", "natural_cut": "Enduring Curiosity"},
    {"card": "Search for Glory", "closes": "tutors", "source": "prompt", "why": "To hand, and it reaches every legendary card here (Krang, Jaws, Bard, Teferi's Ageless Insight and more). It cannot reach Tithe. The goldfish misreads it (see gaps).", "natural_cut": "Enduring Curiosity"}
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {"question": "Does the goldfish's tutor_filter regex read 'a snow permanent card, a legendary card, or a Saga card' as snow-permanent-only?", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "tutor_filter returns (('Snow','Permanent'),). That makes Search for Glory a dead card in its screen, and any 'X card, a Y card' tutor is misread the same way."}
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "The goldfish's tutor policy takes 'the biggest card next turn's mana can pay'. It does not aim at Krang or Tithe, so no row prices the find he asked for.",
    "The goldfish has no opponents. Tithe's Treasure is an authored 50% pay rate, so turning an early Tithe into a turn-6 kill is judgment, not a measurement.",
    "Enduring Curiosity's value in the face of blockers is invisible to the goldfish."
  ]
}
